        "original_id": "393ec37c-92df-553f-960f-49e04ba7334e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ziggy Marley, Flea, John Frusciante, Michael Peter Balzary, Ken Chastain\n- Albums: Dragonfly, Love Is My Religion\n- Bands: Red Hot Chili Peppers, Ziggy Marley & The Melody Makers\n- Songs: Rainbow in the Sky, Melancholy Mood\n- Roles: musician, actor, bassist, percussionist\n\nFacts:\n- Ziggy Marley & The Melody Makers ended in 2000.\n- Dragonfly was Ziggy Marley's first solo album.\n- The song \"Rainbow in the Sky\" on Dragonfly features Flea and John Frusciante of the Red Hot Chili Peppers.\n- The song \"Melancholy Mood\" on Dragonfly features only Flea.\n- Michael Peter Balzary was born on 16 October 1962 and is better known by the stage name Flea.\n- Flea is an Australian-American musician and actor best known as the bassist and a founding member of the Red Hot Chili Peppers.\n- Love Is My Religion was Ziggy Marley's second solo album after Dragonfly.\n- Ken Chastain performed percussion on Ziggy Marley's album Love Is My Religion.",
